1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,780
A stress test says an invented portfolio
of three chip stocks would lose 78%

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,300
in a tech crash.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,300
Where does a number like that come from?

4
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:11,320
I'm Tanmay Kulkarni, for Humanitarians AI.

5
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:16,120
This week I contributed to Mycroft,
an open repository of finance pipelines.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:17,800
The stress test is one of them,

7
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:20,800
and the portfolio is invented,
not investment advice.

8
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:23,540
A scenario is a short
list of named shocks,

9
00:00:23,680 --> 00:00:25,740
each one a percentage hit
to part of the market.

10
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:30,440
This tech crash names four price
shocks: the whole market, −15%;

11
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:33,280
semiconductors, −35; AI stocks,

12
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,220
−40; and technology, −30.

13
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:40,060
The engine's rule is to add up the
shocks that belong to each holding.

14
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,480
The first chip stock
belongs to the market,

15
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,900
to semiconductors, and to the AI list.

16
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,300
15 + 35 + 40 comes to −90.

17
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,080
A second chip stock gets the same 90.

18
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:55,400
The third is off the AI list, so it
gets 50, and that is a different sum.

19
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,340
Now give each its share of
the book: 40%, 30%, 30%.

20
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:02,720
36 + 27 + 15 makes 78.

21
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:07,340
I wrote a Python copy of the adder
and ran it beside the original code.

22
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:10,100
On 24 requests, every number matched.

23
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,940
So next time a stress test gives
you one number, ask what was added.

24
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:17,840
The full film is "The Sum Behind the
Number: Taking Apart a Stress Test".
